  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "LOGNORM.DIST and LOGNORMDIST use CRT ln(x) for the CDF and exp_of_sum in LN(sigma), LN(sqrt(2pi)), LN(x) order for PDF",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20131 and 20430, LOGNORM.DIST(x, mean, standard_dev, cumulative) and LOGNORMDIST(x, mean, standard_dev) (cumulative only) require x > 0 and standard_dev > 0. The CDF evaluates NORM.S.DIST((crt_log(x) - mean) / standard_dev, TRUE) using CRT ln(x) rather than Excel's scalar LN(x) (distinguished at oc3066), while the PDF forms half_square = RN53(RN64(d*d) / RN64(sigma*sigma)) / 2 with d = RN53(RN64(excel_log(x) - mean)) and evaluates excel_exp_of_sum(half_square, [excel_log(sigma), LN_SQRT_2PI, excel_log(x)]), flushing subnormals to 0. All 7,809 LOGNORM.DIST and 3,299 LOGNORMDIST full-bank rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in CalcFunc-Evidence cache/oracle/build-20131/LOGNORM.DIST.jsonl.gz and LOGNORMDIST.jsonl.gz (Excel 16.0 build 20131) and cache/oracle-20430/build-20430/LOGNORM.DIST.jsonl.gz (Excel 16.0 build 20430); 7,809/7,809 LOGNORM.DIST and 3,299/3,299 LOGNORMDIST full-bank rows match.",
